    {
      "text": "Figure 2(e): the completed formalization after a human proved the remaining nodes. Rectangles are definitions and ellipses are theorems; dashed arrows mark a statement-level use and solid arrows a proof-level use. Definition nodes taylorKernel, taylorRemainderKernel, taylorPoly, lineMap and lineCurve sit at the top; the target frechet_taylor_integral is the sink at the bottom. Every theorem node is dark green, meaning the whole graph, including the target frechet_taylor_integral, is proved without sorry.",
